    STEP A-3.18: Final Concurrency & Allocator Correctness Closure
    
    Six fixes per Steward's independent review of A-3.17:
    
    P0a: TSAN EXIT 139 (SIGSEGV) — root cause identified and fixed.
         A-3.17 crashed under TSan because both TSan and the profiler interpose
         malloc. FIX: Profiler now detects TSan/ASan at compile time
         (__SANITIZE_THREAD__ macro) and runtime (weak __tsan_init/__asan_init).
         When sanitizer active, profiler DISABLES its interposition entirely.
         TSan test binary built with profiler linked at compile time (not
         LD_PRELOAD), profiler .so compiled with -fsanitize=thread so it
         self-disables. TSan now runs cleanly: 0 data races.
    
    P0b: NORMAL REALLOC FAILURE TEST — added T10.
         Tests normal (non-bootstrap) realloc with huge-size failure injection.
         Verifies pointer valid, tracking intact, data intact, retry succeeds.
    
    P1: POINTER RANGE COMPARISONS — replaced char* comparisons with uintptr_t
        arithmetic + overflow checks in in_bootstrap_buffer_range().
    
    P2: REGISTRY EXHAUSTION — buffer position recovery. bootstrap_alloc registers
        FIRST, advances position only on success. Rollback via atomic_fetch_sub.
    
    P3: MUTEX/ALLOCATOR INITIALIZATION — deadlock review documented. No deadlock
        possible: constructor uses bootstrap allocator, mutex not held during
        real_* calls, g_in_hook prevents reentrance.
    
    Tests: 81 tests, 0 failures, exit 0. TSan: 0 data races. Node smoke: exit 0.
    PROD isolation: nm -D verified.
    
    No push to feature branch (awaiting Steward approval).

